{"id": "unknown-2026-06-17-014", "date": "2026-06-17", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 25, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.75, "keywords": ["record", "growth"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["情緒極端"]}, "title": "Spain records 397 hours of negatives prices in Q1", "content": "<p>Spain faces a surge in negative electricity prices driven by rapid solar growth outpacing short-term demand, exposing vulnerabilities in merchant renewable projects. Spanish PV association UNEF argues the imbalance is temporary, as new electricity-intensive demand is expected to materialize within 3–5 years.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/17/spain-records-397-hours-of-negatives-prices-in-q1/\">Spain records 397 hours of negatives prices in Q1</a> appeared first on", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/17/spain-records-397-hours-of-negatives-prices-in-q1/", "type": "rss"}]}
